# SushiTrack Python package

The ctypes binding of SushiTrack with the native libraries bundled inside it.

## Contents
```
sushitrack/
    __init__.py
    {runtime_lib}    Native SushiTrack library
    {sushilog_lib}   Native SushiLog library, which SushiTrack logs through
sushitrack.json      Default runtime configuration
example.py           A usage example
LICENSE              The PolyForm Noncommercial licence of SushiTrack
NOTICE.md            The third-party code inside the libraries
licenses/            The licence texts NOTICE.md cites
```

## Quick start
```sh
python example.py
```

## Integrating into your own project
Copy the `sushitrack/` directory into your project, or add it to PYTHONPATH:
```python
from sushitrack import Tracker
tracker = Tracker()
tracks = tracker.update([(x, y, w, h, score, label)], dt=1/30)
```
The binding loads the native libraries from inside the package; no build tree or environment
variable is needed. Ship `LICENSE`, `NOTICE.md` and `licenses/` with any copy of the package.

Platform: {platform}
